The comment `@@@ Bits outside the flipped range are unchanged after flip.` indicates that for any bit index not in the range `[fromIndex, toIndex)`, the value of the bit should remain the same after the `flip` operation.

To express this:
- We need to ensure that for all bit indices `i` such that `i < fromIndex` or `i >= toIndex`, the value of `get(i)` after the flip is equal to its value before the flip.
- We can use `\old(...)` to refer to the value before the method call.
- We use `\forall int i; cond; spec` to express that the condition holds for all such indices.

Note: Since `BitSet` can theoretically have very large indices, we cannot iterate over all integers. However, in practice, the implementation uses a finite array. But for specification purposes, we quantify over all non-negative integers outside the flipped range.

Thus, the correct assertion is:

<code>assert \forall int i; (i >= 0 && i < fromIndex) || (i >= toIndex); this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i));</code>
